            <ArticleTitle>Erratum to: Editorial: Do Orthopaedic Surgeons Belong on the Sidelines at American Football Games?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3118</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11999-017-5508-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the November Editorial, &quot;Editorial: Do Orthopaedic Surgeons Belong on the Sidelines at American Football Games?&quot; a statistic was attributed to a JAMA study (Ref. 10) that should have been attributed to an article from the New York Times (Ref. 16). The sentence in question should read: &quot;We accept that critique, provided that the skeptics acknowledge that the best-case estimate in support of the safety of football would result in a CTE prevalence estimate of 9%, since only another 1200 ex-NFL players have died [16] since this research group [10] began studying football players' brains.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
